  "docs": {
    "holidays": "Holiday windows and strengths are fixed in holiday_short / holiday_block. Offsets are calendar days relative to the closure boundary. Short multipliers use round(exp(0.75*mean_fold_log_residual),4); long1 Seollal radish uses round(exp(0.50*mean_fold_log_residual),4). The validator checks these recipes without selecting the windows or strengths.",
    "methods": "Fixed ExtraTrees / HistGradientBoosting forecasts of log(target/last_price) relative to an EWMA baseline. A|B is an equal log-space blend; h1last uses the last price at horizon 1. No fitting or residual-feedback adaptation occurs during inference.",
    "protocol": "Evaluation of the fixed configuration on 2020-2024 data and verification of its numerical recipes. The script does not search over methods, holiday windows, mixture weights or damping strengths; it does not establish the historical selection procedure. See validation_2020_2024.json diagnostic_scope for the feature implementation and calibration/evaluation overlap.",
    "scales": "The exact configured scale factors are in rules. validate_2020_2024.py checks the stated numerical recipes against 2022-2024 forward-fold residuals. The onion factor is a fixed scale factor, not mean-residual bias centering.",
    "state_space": "Configuration key retained for compatibility. Static volatility damping plog -= lam*vol30^2*(h/10), followed by price-space interpolation with anchor weight w_max*(h/10). This is not a fitted Kalman filter.",
    "submission": "10일 예측 모델. train.py reads only the 2020-2024 training bundle. Observed inference inputs are selected by case with date < origin; public-holiday dates are calendar inputs. Cases and target windows are read from input/cases.json.",
    "volshrink": "Fixed volatility-dependent log-price adjustment plog -= c*vol30^2*h. No claim of MAPE optimality is made."
  },
